      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What event or condition causes the organizer to start the room reservation process — for example, is it triggered by creating a calendar event, receiving a meeting request, or some other action?",
      "answer": "The process starts when the organizer collects the meeting date, time, and participant count. The specific trigger — such as a calendar event creation or an incoming meeting request — is not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "What system or method does the organizer currently use to check room availability — for instance, a shared calendar, a dedicated booking platform, or a physical sign-up sheet?",
      "answer": "The organizer uses a calendar system and a room reservation system to check availability. The exact interface — shared calendar view or dedicated booking platform — is not specified beyond these two systems."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "If the preferred room is not available at the requested time, what steps does the organizer take — do they select an alternative room, propose a different time, or follow an escalation path?",
      "answer": "If no suitable room is available, the workflow flags it as an exception called 'room unavailable.' The specific fallback steps — such as selecting an alternative room or proposing a different time — are not detailed further in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How are participants informed of the confirmed room details — is this done through an automatic calendar invitation, a manual email, a messaging tool, or another channel?",
      "answer": "After reserving the room, the organizer creates or updates a calendar invitation and then notifies participants of the room information using an email or collaboration tool. Whether this notification is automatic or manual is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What is the process when a reserved meeting is cancelled or rescheduled — who is responsible for releasing the room, and how is that action carried out?",
      "answer": "Cancellation or rescheduling is not explicitly detailed in the workflow. A 'reservation conflict' is listed as a recognized exception, but the specific steps, responsible actor, or system actions for releasing a room are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Is any employee permitted to reserve a meeting room, or are there role-based restrictions or an approval step required before a reservation is confirmed?",
      "answer": "The workflow assigns reservation actions solely to the meeting organizer with no mention of role-based restrictions or an approval step. Whether all employees can act as organizers or if there are access restrictions is not specified."
    }
  ]
}
